h(2, id: "cli") { 2. Command line }

p { The binary is named code{docup}. Commands: }

codeblock(lang: "text", file: "usage", line_numbers: true) {!
docup build <input.du> [flags]
docup watch <input.du> [flags]
docup version
docup help
!}

p { code{docup -v} and code{docup --version} print the same string as code{docup version}. code{docup -h} and code{docup --help} print usage. Any other command name is an error. }

p { Color in the terminal is on when stdout is a terminal and code{NO_COLOR} is unset. Otherwise ANSI codes are omitted. }

h(3, id: "flags") { 2.1 Flags }

table {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Flag }
    cell { Meaning }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-o}, code{--output} }
    cell { Output HTML path. Default is the input path with the extension changed to .html. If the input has no extension, code{.html} is appended. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-s}, code{--style} }
    cell { Path to a CSS file. Contents are copied into code{<style id="docup-custom-css">}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-p}, code{--port} }
    cell { Port for the watch-mode server. Default 8080. Must parse as a u16. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-V}, code{--verbose} }
    cell { Print elapsed time for each build stage. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-q}, code{--quiet} }
    cell { Hide stage progress and the success summary. }
  }
}

p { code{--verbose} and code{--quiet} together are an error. A flag that expects a value and does not get one is an error. Unknown flags are an error. Only one input path is accepted. }

h(3, id: "build") { 2.2 build }

p { Compiles once and writes the HTML file. A missing or unreadable input file is a fatal error. An empty file (only ASCII whitespace) is a fatal error. If the input does not use a .du extension, the compiler prints a warning and continues. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup build report.du
docup build report.du -o dist/index.html -s style.css
docup build report.du --verbose
!}

h(3, id: "watch") { 2.3 watch }

p { Compiles once, writes the output file, then binds code{127.0.0.1:<port>}. It polls watched files every 250 ms. On change it rebuilds. A failed rebuild leaves the last page in place and keeps watching. }

p { If the first compile fails, the server still starts. The page body is a short HTML error placeholder until a later compile succeeds. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup watch report.du
docup watch report.du --port 3000
!}

p { Watched paths are the root source file, every successfully resolved include, and the code{--style} file if one was given. }

h(3, id: "dev-server") { 2.4 Dev server }

p { The watch server accepts GET only. Other methods return 405. }

table {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Path }
    cell { Response }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{/}, code{/index.html} }
    cell { Current compiled HTML, with a live-reload EventSource script inserted before code{</body>}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{/docup-events} }
    cell { Server-sent events. A rebuild writes code{data: reload}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { any other path }
    cell { File under the input file's directory, if it exists. Otherwise 404. }
  }
}

p { Asset Content-Type is chosen from the file extension: html, css, js, json, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, svg, webp, ico, woff, woff2, ttf. Anything else is code{application/octet-stream}. }
